      "text": "The docstring of `missingRows_preserved` states a general claim (\"Row replacement preserves NOT NULL even when the row-list count differs\"). The formula is one concrete instance: `missingRows` is not `Database.RowsShaped`, and `NotNull` holds after storing the single row `[.null]` at position 0. Fix: restate the two conjuncts for `missingRows` and the one stored row, and say that the general case is `Database.EachTable.setRows`."
